<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('partials/head', { title: title, description: description, canonical: canonical }) %>
<script type="application/ld+json">
<%- JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'WebApplication', '@id': SITE + '/#app', name: 'MileageLogMaker', url: SITE + '/', applicationCategory: 'FinanceApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any (web browser)',
      description: 'Free mileage log generator. Log business, medical and charity trips and download a PDF log with the IRS rates applied to each trip date. CRA and HMRC versions included.',
      offers: [
        { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'Free', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
        { '@type': 'Offer', name: 'Pro (one-time)', price: '9', priceCurrency: 'USD', url: GUMROAD_URL }
      ] },
    { '@type': 'WebSite', '@id': SITE + '/#website', name: 'MileageLogMaker', url: SITE + '/' },
    { '@type': 'Organization', '@id': SITE + '/#org', name: 'MileageLogMaker', url: SITE + '/', logo: SITE + '/android-chrome-512x512.png' }
  ]
}) %>
</script>
</head>
<body class="has-sticky">

<%- include('partials/nav') %>

<section class="hero">
  <span class="badge">Updated for the July 1, 2026 IRS rate change</span>
  <h1>Free IRS Mileage Log Generator</h1>
  <p class="lead">Add your trips, get a clean PDF mileage log with the date, destination, business purpose and miles the IRS asks for. The right 2026 rate is applied to each trip by date. No signup, no app.</p>
  <div class="rates">
    <div class="rate-card"><strong>76¢</strong><span>business mile from Jul 1, 2026</span></div>
    <div class="rate-card"><strong>72.5¢</strong><span>business mile Jan 1 to Jun 30</span></div>
    <div class="rate-card"><strong>23.5¢ / 20.5¢</strong><span>medical, after / before Jul 1</span></div>
    <div class="rate-card"><strong>14¢</strong><span>charity mile, all year</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="rate-note">Source: <a href="<%= R.SOURCES.irsRates.url %>" rel="noopener" target="_blank">IRS standard mileage rates</a> (Notice 2026-10 and Announcement 2026-11). Last checked <%= R.LAST_CHECKED_TEXT %>. <a href="/mileage-log-2026-irs-rate">What changed in July</a></p>
</section>

<%- include('partials/tool', { region: 'us', purposePlaceholder: 'Client meeting at Acme Co.' }) %>

<section class="section">
  <h2>What your mileage log needs to show</h2>
  <p>IRS Publication 463 asks you to record, for each business use of the car: the <strong>date</strong>, your <strong>business destination</strong>, the <strong>business purpose</strong> and the <strong>miles driven</strong>, plus the <strong>total miles</strong> you drove the car in the year. A log you update at least weekly counts as a timely record. Every PDF from this generator has those columns, your odometer readings and a dated rate summary.</p>
  <p><a href="/irs-mileage-log-requirements">Read the full IRS mileage log requirements with a sample log</a></p>
  <div class="feature-grid">
    <div class="feature"><h3>Rates by trip date</h3><p>2026 trips before July 1 use 72.5¢, later trips 76¢. The PDF shows both subtotals so your preparer can check them.</p></div>
    <div class="feature"><h3>Stays in your browser</h3><p>Trips are saved in this browser. When you download, the PDF is built on our server and not kept there.</p></div>
    <div class="feature"><h3>Canada and UK too</h3><p>Kilometre logbook with business-use % for the <a href="/cra-mileage-log-template">CRA</a>, and an <a href="/mileage-log-uk">HMRC</a> log with the 55p rate from 6 April 2026.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Prefer a printable template?</h2>
  <p>Download a blank log to fill in by hand or in Excel or Google Sheets. The spreadsheets calculate miles from odometer readings and apply the 2026 rate by date.</p>
  <div class="downloads">
    <a class="dl" href="/templates/mileage-log-template-2026.xlsx" download><strong><span class="fmt">XLSX</span>Mileage log 2026</strong><span>IRS columns, formulas, 400 rows</span></a>
    <a class="dl" href="/templates/mileage-log-template-2026.pdf" download><strong><span class="fmt pdf">PDF</span>Printable mileage log</strong><span>Letter size, 21 rows per page</span></a>
    <a class="dl" href="/mileage-log-real-estate-agents#templates"><strong>Real estate agents</strong><span>Property address and client columns</span></a>
    <a class="dl" href="/mileage-log-uber-drivers#templates"><strong>Rideshare and delivery</strong><span>Per-shift odometer log</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Guides for your kind of work</h2>
  <div class="related-grid">
    <a href="/mileage-log-self-employed" class="related-card"><strong>Self-employed and freelancers</strong><span>Schedule C, home office trips</span></a>
    <a href="/mileage-log-real-estate-agents" class="related-card"><strong>Real estate agents</strong><span>Showings, listings, closings</span></a>
    <a href="/mileage-log-uber-drivers" class="related-card"><strong>Uber and Lyft drivers</strong><span>Online miles vs deductible miles</span></a>
    <a href="/mileage-log-doordash-drivers" class="related-card"><strong>DoorDash and delivery</strong><span>Deduction calculator</span></a>
    <a href="/cra-mileage-log-template" class="related-card"><strong>Canada (CRA)</strong><span>Logbook template, simplified logbook</span></a>
    <a href="/mileage-log-uk" class="related-card"><strong>United Kingdom (HMRC)</strong><span>55p / 25p approved rates</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="pricing">
  <h2>Free or Pro</h2>
  <p>The generator is free to use for as many trips as you like. Pro is a single $9 payment for people who hand the log to a client, employer or accountant.</p>
  <div class="pricing">
    <div class="plan">
      <h3>Free</h3>
      <div class="price">$0</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Unlimited trips, saved in your browser</li>
        <li>IRS, CRA and HMRC rates applied by date</li>
        <li>PDF log with a light "Free version" watermark</li>
        <li>Blank Excel and PDF templates</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="#generator" class="btn btn-ghost">Start logging</a>
    </div>
    <div class="plan pro">
      <h3>Pro</h3>
      <div class="price">$9 <small>one-time, no subscription</small></div>
      <ul>
        <li>PDF without the watermark</li>
        <li>Export your trips to Excel and CSV</li>
        <li>Your logo on the PDF</li>
        <li>Activate on any device with your Gumroad license key</li>
      </ul>
      <button type="button" class="btn" onclick="MLM.openPro()">Get Pro for $9</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:14px;font-size:14px">Checkout is handled by Gumroad. Your license key arrives in the Gumroad receipt email.</p>
</section>

<div class="sticky-cta"><a href="#generator" class="btn">Add a trip</a><button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost" onclick="MLM.openPro()">Pro $9</button></div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<%- include('partials/pro-modal') %>
<script>window.MLM_RATES = <%- CLIENT_RATES %>;</script>
<script src="/calc.js?v=2"></script>
<script src="/app.js?v=3"></script>
</body>
</html>
